+updates and additions succeed.  If any one of them fails (for
+example, because the back-end database commit failed), the
+request <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> fail with a 500 (Server Error) response and all
+tentative binding updates <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be removed.</t>
+          </li>
+          <li pn="section-10.3-7.8" derivedCounter="8.">The registrar returns a 200 (OK) response.  The response <bcp14>MUST</bcp14>
